{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Pnp6Juh5xDRMmZqtvWS9Uc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Anchor R&D Surface v3 â€” \"Mission Control\" â€” Planning Trio Summary\n\n**Goal / North Star (locked)**\n- Turn the Anchor dashboard into a durable mission-control for trio-driven R&D, where every project is a thin, full-width row carrying an accurate, auto-generated summary.\n- Clicking any session expands a concise, cached, **in-place** summary â€” showing when it ran, what was asked, the North-Star, clickable doc links, and effort in tokens + time â€” never a separate \"no summary\" page.\n- Trio work runs as persistent, isolated, server-side terminal sessions managed like stacking windows (open / attach / minimize / kill-with-confirm), status-colored, and surviving disconnect â€” so launching a session feels like a real terminal.\n\n**Locked decisions (Stage 0/1 user gates)**\n- **Terminal substrate = real ConPTY** (via `pywinpty`). This consciously waives Anchor's \"stdlib-only / no native assets\" rule **for the terminal subsystem only**; everything else stays stdlib, and the subsystem degrades gracefully (dashboard still works) if `pywinpty` is absent.\n- **Summaries = proactive background generation, cached.** Generated once at discovery/rescan and right after a run completes; clicking shows a ready cached summary in-place, with lazy \"generatingâ€¦\" only as a fallback.\n- **Concurrency isolation = git worktrees per session.** Each plan/research/build session is isolated in its own worktree so concurrent sessions can't dirty one another.\n\n**Member documents (the trio set)**\n- Master Plan (frozen design) â€” this document.\n- Implementation Plan (Foreman-ready).\n- Execution Log.\n\n---\n\nThese claims are drawn directly from the provided anchors and member-document titles. The anchor text for the North Star and the third locked decision is truncated in the source material I was given, so the final clauses of the North Star (\"â€¦feels exactly like a real C[onPTY/terminal]\") and locked decision #3 are summarized only as far as the supplied text grounds them â€” I did not fabricate the cut-off portions."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4310,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34700,"cache_read_input_tokens":20597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":34700},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"caa1257d-7323-4551-a165-064d1a683872","uuid":"e3ddbcef-c391-49eb-8257-af4919c852dd","request_id":"req_011Cc52sCy53YT1WszRL36SR"}
